  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1232 PM CST Tue Nov 24 2026\n\nHigh pressure will keep the weather dry into Thursday morning as\na low pressure system lifts through the middle Atlantic states on\nThanksgiving. The mid level trough associated with the storm will\ntrack through the Ohio Valley during this period, which could\ncause some light rain to scrape the southeastern portion of the\nCWA Thursday afternoon into Friday with light rain. While NBM\nchances for rain during this period are 10-30%, it will be\nfighting dry northeasterly winds with several model solutions\ncompletely dry across our area during this period. Therefore,\nthere is low confidence in seeing rain across east-central\nWisconsin and the lakeshore with at most some light rain or\nsprinkles anticipated if we see rain at all.\n\nA weak system tracking through southern Canada will bring a small\nchance (10-20%) for rain/snow this weekend; however, a blend of \nensembles and NBM suggest the main focus for precip this weekend \nwill stay over Ohio Valley and north across Ontario Canada. High\npressure then keeps the region mainly dry early next week.\n\nTemperatures: Near normal temperatures are expected on Wednesday\nwith highs around 40. Conditions then steadily warm into the 40s \nThanksgiving and into the weekend. Could even see some highs near\n50 degrees on Saturday ahead of a cold front that moves through \nlater in the weekend.",
